<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-tectus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>uncovered</i>,
				<i>unclad.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nuda, intecta corpora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. H. 1, 59</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">semiruta moenia, domūs intectae,</span>”
				<i>unroofed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cetera intecti,</span>”
				<i>with no other covering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. G.
					17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dux prope intectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					5, 22</span></i>
			: pedes, <i>uncovered</i>, i. e. <i>with only sandals on them</i>, <i><span class="en">id. A. 2,
			59</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					4, 77</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nudum et intectum corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 254</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 10</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>unconcealed</i>, <i>open</i>, <i>frank</i> (opp.
			obscurus), <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 4, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
